        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Tin Cup Challenge Q & A</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/49411.webp" alt="Tin Cup Challenge Q & A" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p><strong>Q: What is the Tin Cup Challenge?</strong></p>
<p><strong>A:</strong> One of the most innovative charitable fundraisers in the nation, the Tin Cup Challenge is also one of the most successful. In 2016, the event raised <span><strong>$1,263,829</strong></span> from <span><strong>964</strong></span> donors. Since 2008, this event has raised an astounding <span><strong>$9,546,466</strong></span>, directly benefitting Teton Valley’s cherished nonprofits working tirelessly to enhance our quality of life.</p>
<p><strong>Q: How does it work?</strong></p>
<p><strong>A:</strong> During the 9-week charitable giving period, donors make gifts to the Community Foundation of Teton Valley designating their favorite local nonprofits as recipients. Donors are inspired to give generously, knowing their gifts will be matched by a grant from the Challenger Fund. The 10th Annual Tin Cup Challenge giving period began May 19th and ends July 21st at 5pm. Gifts can be made online at <a href="http://www.tincupchallenge.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">www.tincupchallenge.org</a> or by using the donor forms inserted in the Tin Cup Challenge brochures mailed to each postal box holder in the valley.</p>
<p><strong>Q: Why does it matter?</strong></p>
<p><strong>A:</strong> The Community Foundation of Teton Valley believes deeply that our local nonprofits are the backbone of our community, providing much needed programs and services to Teton Valley residents. The Tin Cup Challenge provides these important grassroots organizations with critical funding, ensuring their sustainability and supporting their efforts to enhance our quality of life.</p>
<p><strong>Q: What is the Challenger Fund?</strong></p>
<p><strong>A:</strong> Challengers are a special group of corporations and individuals who give $1,000 or more to the Challenger Fund each year. Gifts to the Challenger Fund are used to host the Tin Cup Challenge and provide matching grants to participating nonprofits. Challengers are community leaders who promote charitable giving and intrinsically value Teton Valley’s nonprofits. The generosity of our Challengers inspires increased community giving and is the key to the Tin Cup Challenge’s success.</p>
<p><strong>Q: When is this year’s Tin Cup Celebration Day?</strong></p>
<p><strong>A:</strong> The 10th Annual Tin Cup Challenge Celebration Day, taking place Saturday, July 15<sup>th</sup> from 9am-12pm at the Driggs City Plaza, will be fun for the whole family, offering a 5K Fun Run/Walk along with 5K and 10K competitive races for all ages.  The Tin Cup Challenge is a great opportunity to gather with friends, family and neighbors to support Teton Valley nonprofits.  All fun run and race participants will receive a commemorative 10<sup>th</sup> Annual Tin Cup Challenge t-shirt.</p>
<p><strong>Q: What has the Tin Cup Challenge accomplished over the past decade?</strong></p>
<p><strong>A:</strong> The Tin Cup Challenge has promoted unprecedented philanthropy in Teton Valley. One out of every 4 local households now participates in charitable giving through the Tin Cup Challenge, weaving into the fabric of our community a deeply held value of generosity. Anyone who knows Teton Valley, knows we love our nonprofits and the Tin Cup Challenge provides an effective, efficient vehicle for supporting these vital organizations. This program allows our nonprofits to forgo countless amounts of energy and resources fundraising and instead focus on their missions to improve lives in Teton Valley.</p>
